WEBVTT

00:16.180 --> 00:18.220
My brother's medicine...

00:18.760 --> 00:21.729
The medicine Yuke always
arranged for him...

00:21.730 --> 00:24.890
I never realized it was so expensive.

00:25.400 --> 00:30.319
If I'd known, I wouldn't have kept
asking for more without paying him.

00:30.320 --> 00:33.449
Honestly, I disgust myself.

00:33.450 --> 00:37.070
And it was for someone in my family, too.
I'm so awful.

00:37.870 --> 00:40.329
I only understood
after Yuke left the party

00:40.330 --> 00:45.460
just how hard he was always
working to keep us all safe.

00:46.210 --> 00:47.500
Too late, I know.

00:48.080 --> 00:50.209
Oh, I really messed up.

00:50.210 --> 00:52.460
I should have apologized to him sooner.

00:54.010 --> 00:57.139
Yuke is a big softie
when all's said and done.

00:57.140 --> 01:00.259
If I'd sincerely apologized,
he probably would've forgiven me.

01:00.260 --> 01:01.309
And then maybe...

01:01.310 --> 01:07.190
Maybe he even would've
invited me to join Clover.

01:07.810 --> 01:11.269
Nah, I guess that'd be
too convenient, huh?

01:11.270 --> 01:13.490
Never mind. Forget I said that.

01:14.030 --> 01:16.359
Yuke and the other members of Clover

01:16.360 --> 01:19.779
always seem to enjoy themselves,
and they trust each other so much.

01:19.780 --> 01:21.740
They're almost like a family.

01:22.740 --> 01:25.659
I wonder if a future like
that was ever in my cards...

01:25.660 --> 01:27.120
Jamie!

01:28.330 --> 01:34.299
Listen. All of Thunder Pike's evil
deeds are recorded on this magic gem.

01:34.300 --> 01:36.880
I think it'll be useful to you
in some way.

01:37.590 --> 01:40.550
I really am sorry, Yuke.

03:14.980 --> 03:17.569
(Episode 8: One Who Was Once a Friend)
It almost sounds like she's reading her will.

03:17.570 --> 03:19.440
I guess she regretted it all.

03:19.820 --> 03:20.950
I screwed up!

03:21.360 --> 03:24.449
Jamie gave everything to save us,

03:24.450 --> 03:26.450
and I left her to die.

03:26.780 --> 03:28.619
Don't blame yourself.

03:28.620 --> 03:30.960
You didn't have a choice.

03:31.660 --> 03:34.580
I didn't want to tell you about this...

03:35.500 --> 03:38.590
but we got a distress signal
stream from Achromatic Darkness.

03:41.760 --> 03:43.719
...anyone... hear me?

03:43.720 --> 03:44.719
It's Jamie...

03:44.720 --> 03:47.429
Achromatic Darkness is in serious danger.

03:47.430 --> 03:49.600
The floors have started falling apart...

03:50.230 --> 03:54.980
That's definitely Thunder Pike's
Witch, Jamie Osen, right?

03:55.560 --> 03:58.269
They're arguing about whether
we should send help.

03:58.270 --> 04:00.490
Please do! No...

04:01.070 --> 04:02.240
I'll go myself.

04:02.610 --> 04:06.029
Whoa, now.
You haven't fully recovered yet.

04:06.030 --> 04:06.990
Don't be reckless.

04:07.620 --> 04:08.909
Please let me go.

04:08.910 --> 04:10.450
I left her in there.

04:11.790 --> 04:12.870
She's a friend.

04:13.620 --> 04:16.829
Find another Scroll of Exit for me.

04:16.830 --> 04:17.789
I'll pay you.

04:17.790 --> 04:21.260
I'll decide whether we send help or not.

04:25.590 --> 04:27.799
I'll go save her myself.

04:27.800 --> 04:29.059
No, you won't!

04:29.060 --> 04:31.139
We owe Jamie our lives!

04:31.140 --> 04:32.979
I'm going, too.

04:32.980 --> 04:35.439
You'll do something reckless
if you go in alone.

04:35.440 --> 04:37.059
I'll go, too!

04:37.060 --> 04:38.150
And me.

04:38.480 --> 04:42.899
After they put this on me, I was
the one in the most danger.

04:42.900 --> 04:44.650
So I have to go.

04:44.950 --> 04:46.659
Rain, come here a sec.

04:46.660 --> 04:48.160
Huh? Okay...

04:51.290 --> 04:56.580
Warped smile, chains of
despair, crumbling gears...

04:57.080 --> 04:58.290
Dispel Magic.

05:04.470 --> 05:07.799
It came off? I don't know this spell...

05:07.800 --> 05:10.810
I think it's probably dark magic.

05:11.260 --> 05:16.020
It seems like spells and skills I didn't
know before have been forced into me.

05:16.730 --> 05:18.689
That mark...

05:18.690 --> 05:21.690
It looks like I'm a disciple of
the Pale, Immortal Ruler now.

05:21.980 --> 05:23.939
Don't tell the church, okay?

05:23.940 --> 05:25.320
It's not funny.

05:25.700 --> 05:27.659
A-Are you going to be all right?

05:27.660 --> 05:29.570
I'm just fine at the moment.

05:30.160 --> 05:33.580
I guess the goddess of death took
a liking to me, in her own way.

05:35.750 --> 05:37.580
You've all made your stances clear.

05:37.870 --> 05:40.210
Let's go save Jamie!

05:41.090 --> 05:42.709
Hey! Open up!

05:42.710 --> 05:44.839
I know you're back! Open up right now!

05:44.840 --> 05:45.299
- Hey! You hear me?!

05:45.300 --> 05:46.629
- What shall we do?
- Hey! You hear me?!

05:46.630 --> 05:47.339
- Hey! You hear me?!

05:47.340 --> 05:48.089
- I suppose there's no need to ask.

05:48.090 --> 05:48.840
- Hey!
- I suppose there's no need to ask.

05:49.300 --> 05:50.680
Hey—er...

05:51.140 --> 05:54.139
For crying out loud! You should've
opened up right away!

05:54.140 --> 05:57.849
I'm about to be
you guys' master, after all!

05:57.850 --> 06:00.609
Sorry, but could you
stay out of our house?

06:00.610 --> 06:02.610
How dare you give me that attitude?!

06:09.660 --> 06:13.909
If you're holding out hope for Simon,
you should reconsider.

06:13.910 --> 06:15.119
He's dead.

06:15.120 --> 06:19.039
But... I'm sure
he fulfilled our objective!

06:19.040 --> 06:20.750
Rain! Get out here!

06:21.080 --> 06:25.170
I knew it. You're the sponsor
with a grudge against me.

06:25.630 --> 06:28.259
And you're the one who set him
up with the illegal artifact.

06:28.260 --> 06:30.760
Rain! Rain!

06:32.890 --> 06:34.509
Rain!

06:34.510 --> 06:36.810
That's it. Come over here.

06:37.270 --> 06:38.770
Rain!

06:39.810 --> 06:41.270
Hikakiborg?!

06:42.560 --> 06:43.979
R-Rain?

06:43.980 --> 06:45.150
Serves him right.

06:47.240 --> 06:49.399
He's an important merchant.

06:49.400 --> 06:52.160
Killing him would cause a lot of trouble.

06:52.490 --> 06:55.870
I'll stop, then. I don't want
to make trouble for you.

06:58.500 --> 07:01.000
Wh-What did I do to—

07:02.040 --> 07:05.839
You had them put this
thing on me, didn't you?

07:05.840 --> 07:07.170
Th-That's...

07:07.510 --> 07:08.510
You can have it.

07:12.340 --> 07:14.389
Know that the next time I see you,

07:14.390 --> 07:17.679
you're going to die the worst
death you can imagine.

07:17.680 --> 07:19.889
I-I...

07:19.890 --> 07:23.440
Rain! I just... want you to...

07:23.770 --> 07:26.070
Don't speak to me like we're friends.

07:28.820 --> 07:31.900
I belong to Yuke now.

07:34.120 --> 07:37.539
N-No... You're lying!

07:37.540 --> 07:40.250
Let me give you one more little treat.

07:40.620 --> 07:44.210
Cursed princess, cast a
shadow over his heart.

07:44.750 --> 07:48.550
Pour boiling oil into the blood
of any who violate the precepts.

07:51.300 --> 07:55.760
I made it so your blood will boil and
you'll die if you come near Rain.

07:56.300 --> 07:57.180
So...

07:58.310 --> 08:00.020
You'd best watch yourself.

08:01.980 --> 08:06.359
Marina, Nene, could you guys hand
him over to the royal examiner?

08:06.360 --> 08:07.439
With pleasure!

08:07.440 --> 08:08.770
We're on it!

08:11.070 --> 08:13.910
All of our weapons and armor are ready.

08:14.200 --> 08:16.489
I got all the medicinal stuff!

08:16.490 --> 08:18.119
We're good on food, too.

08:18.120 --> 08:19.910
We could leave right now!

08:20.410 --> 08:24.459
No, we don't have the Scroll of Exit yet.
That's the most important thing.

08:24.460 --> 08:26.959
You think the guild master
hasn't found one yet?

08:26.960 --> 08:28.540
They're pretty rare.

08:30.710 --> 08:32.919
I am Lucent of Scordia.

08:32.920 --> 08:34.800
Is Yuke Feldio in there?

08:35.300 --> 08:36.550
Lucent?

08:40.390 --> 08:44.940
This is the first time we've
met in person, Yuke Feldio.

08:45.440 --> 08:47.440
I heard you were looking for this.

08:47.860 --> 08:49.689
A Scroll of Exit...

08:49.690 --> 08:53.279
Do you intend to go into
Achromatic Darkness again?

08:53.280 --> 08:54.570
I do.

08:54.900 --> 08:58.820
Then I ask you: Why are you
going into Achromatic Darkness?

08:59.370 --> 09:01.080
To save a friend.

09:01.790 --> 09:04.290
She saved our lives.

09:05.120 --> 09:07.080
I have to go to her.

09:09.710 --> 09:10.880
Good. Then go.

09:11.300 --> 09:12.509
Um...

09:12.510 --> 09:16.970
You understand what's most important
to an adventurer. That's enough.

09:17.390 --> 09:19.600
If you're going to get her back,
get to it.

09:21.100 --> 09:22.470
Thank you!

09:24.390 --> 09:26.639
I've heard that when
Lucent was starting out,

09:26.640 --> 09:30.439
half of his party was
wiped out in a dungeon.

09:30.440 --> 09:32.480
Oh. So that's why...

09:33.360 --> 09:36.070
We might still make it in time.

09:39.780 --> 09:42.240
It's been decided that Achromatic
Darkness will be sealed.

09:42.660 --> 09:47.830
If you try to force your way in,
my position will demand that I punish you.

09:48.290 --> 09:49.669
You still intend to go?

09:49.670 --> 09:51.999
Of course. If I back out now,

09:52.000 --> 09:54.010
I don't deserve to be an adventurer.

09:54.380 --> 09:57.090
You're every bit as stubborn as Saga.

09:58.130 --> 10:02.599
But do you think you'll
be able to locate Jamie?

10:02.600 --> 10:04.639
I think it'll work out.

10:04.640 --> 10:07.640
I put together all we've learned
about Achromatic Darkness,

10:08.640 --> 10:13.439
and it's a dungeon that leads to
completely different places—

10:13.440 --> 10:16.649
in other words, different worlds—
from common areas like stairways.

10:16.650 --> 10:18.530
That's your interpretation?

10:18.990 --> 10:24.790
And I think where we end up is determined
by the adventurer's own subconscious.

10:25.450 --> 10:27.999
When the two of you went
into Achromatic Darkness,

10:28.000 --> 10:33.790
you thought of it as the most difficult
dungeon—the deepest place there is.

10:34.210 --> 10:35.300
That's true.

10:35.710 --> 10:38.050
And you think the dungeon
responded to that?

10:38.380 --> 10:41.930
I see. So that's why, when you went
in looking for abnormalities,

10:42.140 --> 10:46.390
you immediately wound up in the most
abnormal place of all, the Grey Field.

10:47.060 --> 10:49.099
We'll take advantage of that

10:49.100 --> 10:52.769
and get the dungeon to take us
straight to where Jamie is.

10:52.770 --> 10:56.190
We'll all go in with unwavering
intentions of saving Jamie.

10:58.280 --> 10:59.570
All right.

11:01.610 --> 11:05.450
Be careful. I'll have a
rescue team on standby.

11:05.870 --> 11:09.080
Get some booze and snacks ready
for a celebratory toast, too.

11:09.370 --> 11:10.580
Leave it all to me.

11:11.370 --> 11:12.580
Okay, ready to go?

11:14.500 --> 11:16.210
Let's have fun, but be careful!

11:17.320 --> 11:20.089
(Hectoeyes)

11:20.090 --> 11:22.010
Ready... Go!

11:23.050 --> 11:24.469
Critical Weapon!

11:24.470 --> 11:25.759
Enchant Saint!

11:25.760 --> 11:27.220
Flame Scratch!

11:27.530 --> 11:29.430
(Critical Weapon) (Enchant Saint)
(Flame Scratch)

11:29.730 --> 11:30.980
Magic Blade!

11:38.570 --> 11:41.149
Earth, cast stones upon the sinners!

11:41.150 --> 11:42.570
Stone Bullet!

11:44.700 --> 11:46.450
Master, finish them off!

11:46.780 --> 11:47.580
I'm on it!

11:57.170 --> 11:58.920
Okay, let's keep moving.

12:04.550 --> 12:09.100
Please, skip us to where Jamie is.

12:09.850 --> 12:10.850
I see something!

12:11.180 --> 12:14.190
Please don't let it be
the Grey Field again!

12:16.150 --> 12:18.860
Looks like the skip was successful.

12:19.480 --> 12:21.359
This place looks scary.

12:21.360 --> 12:25.490
It's all broken up, but...
it's Finis, right?

12:25.910 --> 12:28.490
Let's find Jamie quickly and get out.

12:30.200 --> 12:32.000
A blood trail...

12:32.660 --> 12:34.250
It leads that way.

12:34.830 --> 12:36.669
I know where Jamie went!

12:36.670 --> 12:37.750
Where is she?

12:39.800 --> 12:41.380
She headed for the house
where her brother is!

12:42.300 --> 12:43.260
Jamie!

12:46.050 --> 12:47.640
It's that apartment!

12:49.100 --> 12:49.970
Jamie!

12:50.770 --> 12:52.140
Hey, Yuke.

12:53.140 --> 12:56.650
You saved me a lot of trouble
by coming to me yourself.

12:57.900 --> 13:00.979
Simon! Why are you...?

13:00.980 --> 13:04.400
Who knows? Does it even matter?

13:04.650 --> 13:06.910
No... You should be dead!

13:07.660 --> 13:10.660
That thing is not of this world.

13:11.120 --> 13:13.160
It's just like the Shadow Stalker!

13:15.410 --> 13:16.619
So that's it.

13:16.620 --> 13:17.749
Yuke?

13:17.750 --> 13:21.209
Among the artifacts Besio offered up

13:21.210 --> 13:24.049
were several dangerous ones
that could've done this.

13:24.050 --> 13:27.180
He turned himself undead
so he could stay alive?

13:29.050 --> 13:31.809
Now, it's time for you to repent.

13:31.810 --> 13:34.560
Yuke! Apologize with your death!

13:37.440 --> 13:38.399
Marina!

13:38.400 --> 13:40.189
Physical Enchant!

13:40.190 --> 13:41.800
(Enhanced Arm Strength)
(Enhanced Leg Strength) (Enhanced Stamina)

13:43.570 --> 13:45.650
Stay out of my way!

13:54.870 --> 13:57.080
That... hurts!

14:00.000 --> 14:01.249
He's...

14:01.250 --> 14:02.339
His arm...

14:02.340 --> 14:05.340
I'm immortal now, you see.

14:05.800 --> 14:08.629
Lucky you, Yuke. It's so unfair.

14:08.630 --> 14:12.599
Why do all the ladies fawn over you?

14:12.600 --> 14:16.100
I'm so jealous. I envy you!

14:16.640 --> 14:18.599
Which is why, Yuke...

14:18.600 --> 14:22.149
I want to take everything from
you and trample you under my heel.

14:22.150 --> 14:23.479
That's fine, right?

14:23.480 --> 14:26.780
Right, Yuke?!

14:27.320 --> 14:28.239
Check!

14:28.240 --> 14:29.700
Scroll of Light Shield!

14:33.200 --> 14:36.540
Simon... Simon is no longer human.

14:36.950 --> 14:40.040
I have to strike this thing
down and rescue Jamie!

14:42.790 --> 14:44.210
Snare!

14:46.960 --> 14:49.879
Earth, pierce the enemy
with your stone fangs!

14:49.880 --> 14:51.510
- Rock Break!
- Dryads!

14:52.640 --> 14:53.970
This will not—

14:56.890 --> 14:58.769
Yuke!

14:58.770 --> 15:00.730
Simon!

15:04.820 --> 15:08.490
You're wasting your time!
I've reached the highest heights!

15:09.190 --> 15:12.199
With this immortal body,
no one can defeat me.

15:12.200 --> 15:13.869
I fear no one!

15:13.870 --> 15:14.869
Simon!

15:14.870 --> 15:18.619
Yuke, mark my words! I am going
to kill you and your friends!

15:18.620 --> 15:22.119
I will see that you pay
for leaving me to die!

15:22.120 --> 15:24.500
Simon, you...

15:29.470 --> 15:30.880
Scent of decaying roses...

15:31.380 --> 15:33.389
- Sea that swallows the
sun as the black dog howls...

15:33.390 --> 15:35.389
- Nothing you try will do any good!
- Sea that swallows the
sun as the black dog howls...

15:35.390 --> 15:39.640
With the mingling of black and white,
souls vanish into chaos!

15:40.390 --> 15:42.650
Take this! Grade 5 Magic...

15:44.150 --> 15:46.900
Prismatic Missile!

15:52.490 --> 15:55.450
What did I tell you? I won't die.

15:55.820 --> 15:58.700
Then get a good taste of it
with your immortal body.

16:05.290 --> 16:08.460
What is this?! It hurts!

16:08.960 --> 16:10.590
You're not going to finish him?

16:11.220 --> 16:14.179
If he could die, he'd be dead by now.

16:14.180 --> 16:15.589
What did you do to me?!

16:15.590 --> 16:19.469
Theoretically, that spell remains
active until the target dies.

16:19.470 --> 16:23.600
I used the power of Persephone's
curse to modify Prismatic Missile.

16:24.230 --> 16:27.480
Yuke! Aren't we friends?

16:27.820 --> 16:30.480
Yuke! Yuke!

16:37.410 --> 16:38.700
How is she, Rain?

16:39.870 --> 16:42.199
Her wound is deep.

16:42.200 --> 16:43.410
Yuke...

16:44.370 --> 16:45.120
Jamie!

16:47.420 --> 16:48.630
Yuke, it's you.

16:49.210 --> 16:50.549
Any healing potions left?

16:50.550 --> 16:52.880
Yes, but...

16:55.220 --> 16:57.140
The wound isn't closing.

16:57.590 --> 17:00.140
The result of Simon's Magic Blade.

17:00.680 --> 17:03.229
I'm... done for.

17:03.230 --> 17:04.350
No, you're not!

17:05.810 --> 17:11.780
I don't even know if this mark
Persephone put on me is magic or not.

17:12.360 --> 17:13.650
But with this...

17:14.150 --> 17:15.490
Dispel Magic.

17:19.030 --> 17:21.540
The spell is working...

17:24.910 --> 17:26.250
Yuke...

17:29.840 --> 17:31.129
Jamie!

17:31.130 --> 17:33.210
I think she'll be okay now.

17:40.930 --> 17:42.640
Okay. Let's go back.

17:43.310 --> 17:45.140
We should probably hurry.

18:04.910 --> 18:09.120
He's going to be stuck here
suffering forever, isn't he?

18:10.330 --> 18:12.340
I made sure of it.

18:14.710 --> 18:16.050
And...

18:18.470 --> 18:21.050
And now I'm going to leave him behind.

18:22.600 --> 18:24.430
Check! Scroll of Exit!

18:27.640 --> 18:31.310
Goodbye, creature that was once Simon.

18:32.270 --> 18:36.440
Goodbye to one who was once my friend.

18:38.520 --> 18:40.319
(One week later)

18:40.320 --> 18:41.200
Yuke.

18:41.530 --> 18:45.619
I'm sorry, but I have to punish Clover.

18:45.620 --> 18:48.960
Of course. We entered a dungeon
that was to be sealed.

18:49.250 --> 18:51.579
Clover's score will be reduced,

18:51.580 --> 18:53.710
and you're forbidden from
party activity for a month.

18:54.000 --> 18:54.959
That's all?

18:54.960 --> 19:00.379
In addition, my pay will be reduced for
three months for my lack of oversight.

19:00.380 --> 19:01.470
And...

19:02.260 --> 19:05.469
Jamie Osen, formerly of Thunder Pike.

19:05.470 --> 19:06.640
Yes?

19:06.970 --> 19:09.769
You are stripped of your
qualification to be an adventurer

19:09.770 --> 19:12.400
and banned from re-registering
for one year.

19:12.810 --> 19:14.900
And... that's all?

19:15.150 --> 19:16.019
Yes.

19:16.020 --> 19:19.280
But I was a member of Thunder Pike.

19:19.820 --> 19:22.159
I thought I'd be exiled from the kingdom.

19:22.160 --> 19:26.539
You provided proof of Thunder
Pike's illegal activities,

19:26.540 --> 19:29.709
and it was confirmed that you didn't
make any discriminatory statements.

19:29.710 --> 19:31.040
So there you have it.

19:32.670 --> 19:34.130
Thank you!

19:35.960 --> 19:37.300
It's just about winter now.

19:37.710 --> 19:40.549
You put in a good word for me, didn't you?

19:40.550 --> 19:43.679
So that I wouldn't be exiled.

19:43.680 --> 19:45.469
Well, yeah...

19:45.470 --> 19:48.310
But it was the guild and the
kingdom that made the decision.

19:48.600 --> 19:51.729
Yeah. Also, I'm sorry.

19:51.730 --> 19:54.560
Clover shouldn't have been punished.

19:54.900 --> 19:57.570
How many times do you have
to apologize for that?

19:57.860 --> 19:59.070
I mean...

19:59.480 --> 20:01.070
As many times as it takes!

20:01.450 --> 20:04.700
I know a lot happened, but you
can stop worrying about it.

20:06.490 --> 20:08.699
Ugh, this seriously sucks!

20:08.700 --> 20:12.330
I hate myself for taking advantage
of your kindness for so long!

20:12.830 --> 20:14.579
And for staying in that party,

20:14.580 --> 20:16.790
and for laughing at you...

20:17.250 --> 20:19.209
I honestly disgust myself!

20:19.210 --> 20:20.089
Jamie...

20:20.090 --> 20:22.549
And I hate that
womanizing part of you, too.

20:22.550 --> 20:24.839
Th-That's not what I'm trying to do!

20:24.840 --> 20:26.850
And I hate myself for being so easy.

20:27.800 --> 20:30.059
Do you think I can change?

20:30.060 --> 20:32.310
You've changed more than enough already.

20:32.810 --> 20:35.980
I mean, you're talking to me right
now like it's totally normal.

20:38.150 --> 20:41.610
Maybe I should've tried
to communicate better.

20:42.570 --> 20:46.070
If I could've made the effort to
get you guys to understand me,

20:46.950 --> 20:49.080
maybe this would've ended differently.

20:50.490 --> 20:52.249
It's not your fault.

20:52.250 --> 20:54.869
Simon and the rest of us
are the ones to blame.

20:54.870 --> 20:56.670
Are you trying to console me?

20:58.840 --> 21:01.629
Well, ready to head home?

21:01.630 --> 21:03.089
Your brother's waiting, right?

21:03.090 --> 21:04.470
Yeah, he is.

21:08.970 --> 21:11.560
Thank you, Yuke. I mean it.

21:15.690 --> 21:18.149
Well, guess I'll go home, too.

21:18.150 --> 21:19.900
They're all waiting for me.

21:21.610 --> 21:23.489
Welcome home, Yuke!

21:23.490 --> 21:24.399
Welcome home.

21:24.400 --> 21:26.110
We've been waiting for you!

22:56.870 --> 22:59.289
Next time, "A Six-Leaf Clover."

22:59.290 --> 23:01.290
(A Six-Leaf Clover)
